    "judgment": {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "Each selection is mathematically correct and supported by its own captured worked solution. q-105398: write A=I+N, where N²=0; then A⁻¹=I-N, reversing the two off-diagonal signs. q-135373: A²=I, so A⁻¹=A. q-95080: substitution gives e^(s²+2s), whose derivative is 2(s+1)e^(s²+2s). q-95084: substitution gives cot(2s), whose derivative is -2csc²(2s). q-95121: differentiating x ln(x+x²) gives ln(x+x²)+(1+2x)/(1+x) on its real domain. q-95119: differentiating cos(x²+1/x) gives (1/x²-2x)sin(x²+1/x); combining fractions gives exactly option 3. q-37201: differentiating s²sin²(t)-2t²sin²(s) with t fixed gives 2s sin²(t)-4t²sin(s)cos(s); the double-angle identity gives option 2. q-94747: differentiating e^(-st)+e^(st) with t fixed gives t(e^(st)-e^(-st)). q-94813: substitution gives e^(2s+t²), whose t derivative is 2t e^(2s+t²). q-94811: substitution gives 4s+3t-2s²+2t², whose t derivative is 4t+3. q-122599: the gradient is (2,4)/(2x+4y), equivalent to option 4 on 2x+4y>0. q-122617: the three partial derivatives are 2xz+y³, 3xy²-z⁴, and x²-4yz³. q-122407: the gradient (2x,-1) gives vectors (-4,-1), (0,-1), and (4,-1) at the displayed points, matching option 0. q-122619: the gradient (1,2y) gives vectors (1,2), (1,2), and (1,-2), matching option 0. No mathematical disagreement or authored mathematical error was found in these solutions.",
